## 1) MySQL Setup
```sql
CREATE DATABASE cinebook_db;
USE cinebook_db;
```

Then import the schema and seed files:
```bash
mysql -u root -p < database/schema.sql
mysql -u root -p < database/seed.sql
```

## 2) Backend Setup
Open `backend/cinebook-api/src/main/resources/application.properties` and update username/password:
```properties
spring.datasource.username=root
spring.datasource.password=root
```

Run backend:
```bash
cd backend/cinebook-api
mvn clean install
mvn spring-boot:run
```

Backend API runs at:
```text
http://localhost:8080/api
```

## 3) Frontend Setup
```bash
cd frontend
npm install
cp .env.example .env
npm run dev
```

The frontend runs at:
```text
http://localhost:5173
```

## 4) Default Login
- Admin: `admin@cinebook.com` / `admin123`
- User: `user@cinebook.com` / `user123`

## 5) Demo Flow
1. Signup or login
2. Browse movies and select one
3. Choose theatre and showtime
4. Select seats
5. Proceed to payment simulation
6. Confirm booking and view My Bookings

## 6) Useful Commands
```bash
# Backend build
cd backend/cinebook-api
mvn test

# Frontend build
cd frontend
npm run build
```

## 7) Notes
- The frontend includes both backend API integration and local demo fallbacks for development without a running backend.
- This project is suitable for a third-year Information Technology mini-project.
- All major features are implemented in a clean, modular structure.

